 ## Changelog
 
+- 2026-10-20 (6): LoD off = real water everywhere, no water ring (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen in game; `world::chunks::tests::water_is_drawn_only_within_its_range` gained one assert; run `cargo test --lib --release chunks` and the pipeline shader test first).
+    - Cause: the real water was always cut at `WATER_RANGE` (12 blocks), in the section set (`ChunkManager::wet`) and per pixel in `fs_water`, because the LoD's water sheet is what draws the sea beyond it. With the LoD switched off (`Settings::lod`, Options) nothing drew beyond 12 blocks: a ring of water round the player and bare floor outside it.
+    - Fix, one radius with two users: `lib.rs` computes `wr = WATER_RANGE` with the LoD on and `1e9` with it off, and passes it to `ChunkManager::update_visible` (`wet` = `visible` when it is large) and to `ChunkPipeline::frame` (`Uniforms::fogp.y`, which `fs_water` reads instead of the old compile-time `@WR@`). The LoD-on path is unchanged: same constant, same complement with the sheet.
+    - ponytail / UNVERIFIED: at the very edge of the render distance a water section can be drawn whose floor section is just outside the range (the floor and the water are cut by the same box but the occlusion walk may differ); there the fog is ~100% so it should read as fog colour, check it on a device. Real water is now sorted far to near over the whole ring instead of 12 blocks (more page switches, one draw per section run as before).
 - 2026-10-20 (5): options + game menu from b1.7.3 (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen in game; new tests: `options::tests::*` (5), `touch_ui::tests::paused_presses_are_taps_on_the_game_menu`; the 3 pause-menu tests of `touch_ui` that tested the old buttons are gone).
     - New `options.rs`: `GameSettings` (all 13 `EnumOptions`, `options.txt` in the app's storage in the Java format: `music:`, `mouseSensitivity:`, `viewDistance:`, `key_key.forward:` ...), `GuiOptions` (Music, Sound, Invert Mouse, Sensitivity as `GuiSlider`, Difficulty, Video Settings..., Controls..., Done), `GuiVideoSettings` (Graphics, Render Distance, Smooth Lighting, Performance, 3D Anaglyph, View Bobbing, GUI Scale, Advanced OpenGL), `GuiControls` (10 key buttons, tap = `> W <`), `GuiIngameMenu` ("Game menu", Back to game, Achievements + Statistics greyed out, Options..., Save and quit to title, "Saving level.." for the first second, the world is written as it opens). Texts are `en_US.lang`'s. The title screen's "Options..." is the same `OptionsUi`.
     - Replaced: the pause menu of `build_hud` + its `LayoutRects` (`resume`, `reset`, `quit`, `pregen`, `fly`, `dbg`) and `PointerRole`s. While paused every press but the pause button is a `Tap` for `options::Pause` (GUI units, `ScaledResolution`). The TEMPORARY Reset world button is deleted (`take_reset`, `reset_armed`); `reset_world(wipe)` keeps its parameter, no caller passes true any more. The death screen is the same `Pause` (`PauseInfo.dead`: "You died!", Respawn).
